<title>BELGIUM: EU says to assess BT/MCI merger, no other comment.</title>
<headline>EU says to assess BT/MCI merger, no other comment.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission will assess the merger between British Telecommunications Plc and MCI of the United States, the spokesman for European Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The only thing I can say is that it will have to be examined by the Commission,&quot; the spokesman said in reply to reporters's questions.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm not saying it looks complicated or not,&quot; he added. He declined to elaborate on whether the $20 billion deal, which was announced on Sunday, will fall under the European Union's fast-track merger rules.</p>
<p>BT's head of European Union affairs Larry Stone told Reuters earlier today he was confident the operation will be cleared by the Commission, the EU's competition watchdog.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
